pi git guard policy marker: this session blocks ALL GitHub access (--no-git).

bwrap-pi.sh bind-mounts this file at /etc/pi-git-policy inside --no-git sessions,
over the read-only root filesystem. The git/gh policy wrappers treat the marker's
presence as "blocked" and ignore $PI_GIT_GUARD, so an agent that exports
PI_GIT_GUARD=restricted inside the sandbox cannot downgrade the policy.

No GitHub credentials are bound in these sessions either (no gh config, no
git credentials, and no ssh access: the host's /run is hidden behind a tmpfs),
so the env layers (GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=file, the empty GH_CONFIG_DIR) are
belt-and-suspenders rather than the load-bearing wall.

Do not delete this file from the repo: without it the marker mount has no source.
